YAFAP: compmstr-arc-hum-fem-neu

Finally, after years and years of playing this game, I got an
ascension.  A while ago, I decided that I was going to ascend an
Archeologist as my first ascension, and some 100 games or so later, I
got it. I had one character before this up to the Plane of Air, but
didn't have levitation, so that ended with a Jabberwock.

I got off to a pretty regular start, started hitting stuff in the head
with a pickaxe as soon as possible, found a few darts on a kobold
corpse to throw at the more dangerous stuff, and headed down.

I stopped by in the Gnomish Mines, on the first level of the mines, I
had a pretty close call with about 5 gnomes and a few dwarves.  I got
a mattock which lasted until I found a good artifact.  Luckily, the
down stairs were two squares away from the up stairs on a dark level.
I ended up leaving a bit of a stash (mainly the tinning kit and a few
spellbooks I had already read) just above the mines so I could carry
all of the stuff I found in the mines without leaving a stash down
there. I found a magic whistle that I put away until I could find
another pet (my cat having been left on dlvl 1).  The mines above
minetown also provided me with a Magic Marker, which would help me for
a good while through the game.

The Minetown tool shop had a bag of holding in it, so I grabbed that,
and moved all of my stuff into it.  I also picked up that most useful
of items, a towel, and kept it for later when I would inevitably need
it.  I then headed down furthur into the mines to find my luckstone.
After some overly friendly killer bees, and some detours through
trapdoors, I found a luckstone even before the bottom of the mines,
but kept on for the loot/experience.

I found my first unicorn horn down at the bottom of the mines, and so
I could clear out some potions from my bag of holding.

After the mines, I found a bookstore pretty soon, oddly enough, with a
floating eye for a customer before me.  I found a few id scrolls (the
cheapest ones), and left before the mimics could catch up to me.  It
turns out I had already picked up a scroll of charging previously, and
with having a magic marker, that helped me out throughout the game a
whole lot.  I also ended up iding some scrolls of enchant weapon and
armor, so I wrote a few more enchant scrolls, a few more charging
scrolls, buffed up my mattock and my armor a bit, and continued on.

I ended up finding a cloak of protection and (I didn't id them at the
time, but came back for them before taking on rodney) a pair of
jumping boots in a store.

As it turns out, I had found a reflection amulet earlier on as well as
my BoH, but I ran through most of soko as well, just to find loot and
food.  I ended up finding a new pet kitty there.  After I left soko, I
did some IDing and polypiling, making sure my pet was on top of the
pile when I zapped, so I ended up with a pet Silver Dragon which I
promply named Squishy ^^.

I tried to get as many resist intrisics as possible (had a bad run in
with asmodeus' freezeing on a prior game).  I also tinned as many more
of those kinds of corpses as possible, in case of lost intrisics.

I totally lucked out on dlvl 23, thanks to the player stth.  His
corpse got me grayswandir (granted it was cursed and +0, but I
remedied that), a Hawaiian shirt, a cloak of magic resistance, the orb
of weight, speed boots, a bunch of scrolls, holy water, potions,
rings, wands, etc.  He practically handed my most of the ascension
kit, no wishes required.  He had apparently choked on a rothe corpse
that game (looked up only game he got to dlvl 23 on nao)

At this point, I had slow digestion, regeneration when I needed it, a
ring of protection, more holy water than I knew what to do with, and a
good few scrolls to write.  I just had to find a form of confusion to
be able to fooproof all of my armor/weapons, and I ended up looking
until one of my spells was expired.

On the next level, I found a few dragons, was able to make some gray
dragon scale mail, so I ended up with an amulet of reflection, gdsm,
and most of the resistances covered (disintegration, cold, shock, fire
when I found a pyrolisk).

I went ahead and did the quest at this point (the first time I had
done the quest on an Arc, second time ever).  Plus, I sat on the
throne on the main quest level, and got my first ever throne wish (I
got 2 others this game as well, one in the castle, and one on Vlad's
throne).  I ended up with a ring of levitation from this, so that I
could get past medusa and I could sneak in the back of the castle.  I
ended up being able to save most of the wishes from the wand in the
castle for later in the game, as I had most of my kit already.

In the castle, I went through as far as I could, and read a confused,
blessed scroll of taming, converting about half of the room into my
pets, which seems to have worked very well.  The only difficult part
was getting just Squishy to follow me into the valley of the dead.

Good ol' Squishy killed the priest in the valley of the dead, so I
ended up with a robe, and a wished for helm of brilliance, which
allowed me to use Magic mapping (wished for the spellbook) throughout
gehennon to find exits.  After a few levels of this and running out of
pw, I ended up wishing for the eye of tapioca as well, which ended up
just about finishing my ascension kit, as I had previously saved a set
of silver dragon scales, which I could replace my amulet of reflection
with.  I  genocided Liches and Mind flayers ('L' and 'h', using
blessed genocide), so it wasn't that hard getting down to find the
vibrating square.  Unfortunatly, along the way, my loyal and faithful
squishy got killed by one of the demon lords, so I wished for a
blessed archon figurine, and got a new, better squishy, who ended up
taking out vlad before I even got into the room.

I got out of the mazes running into rodney once or twice, and having
the mysterious force knocking me back to the same level (moved 0)
about 4 times in a row.  I had 6 cursed potions of gain level to start
off the climb, which helped a whole lot.  The only issue I had on the
elemental planes was water, it took me a loong time to re-find that
portal (it ended up having an item on top of it hiding it even when I
did find it), and squishy had to be left behind.

On the astral plane, I ended up facing off with Pestilence first,
after taking out the others with a cockatrice corpse that was my last
wish, aided by my handy-dandy Unicorn horn, I made it to the altar, to
find it wasn't the one I needed, so I headed back out, and went to
Death's corner next, where I ended up using a teleport wand to get
things out of the way, and jumping across to the temple.  I was about
dead at this point, so I just ran as fast as I could to the altar,
with death right behind me, and very, very luckily for me, it was the
right altar, so I #offered, and won the game... finally.
I just realized I forgot I had a wand of deah in my bag that could
have taken out Pestilence so much easier than the way I did it.

